From f06b66a3771ff1b50bb2e2cae9d051527774eae5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:24:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] Blaze: full heat2 response encoder for Blaze 3.x
 clients (Madden/NHL)

Heat2Writer now serializes a whole TdfField model in heat2 (structs, lists, maps,
unions, strings, ints) mirroring the heat1 path. A per-connection User.IsHeat2 flag is
set from the preAuth BSDK version (major >= 3) and surfaced to BlazeMessage.Serialize
via an AsyncLocal set in DispatchPacket, so a Blaze 3.x connection's responses are all
heat2 without threading a flag through every handler. preAuth is rebuilt in heat2 for
such clients (heat1 clients keep the cached bytes). Heat1 clients (NBA Jam/Skate 3)
never set the flag, so their path is unchanged.

Verified 2026-11-07 (replay + live): Madden's preAuth response round-trips as valid
heat2 (CIDS list, CONF map, nested QOSS struct, SVER). Live, Madden now consumes
preAuth + 8 fetchClientConfig responses with zero server errors and shows "connecting
to the EA Servers". It then waits after fetchClientConfig -- next blocker is config
*content* (we return empty OSDK_* configs) and/or QoS, which need a heat2 request
decoder + the real config keys Madden expects (reverse-engineering, not encoding).
